Package: Entropy
Type: Package
Title: Entropy Estimation for Seurat and AnnData Objects
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aryan", "Kamal", email = "aryan.kamal@embl.de", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Charles", "Dussiau", email = "charles.dussiau@embl.de", role = c("aut")),
    person("Amelia", "Kurti", email = "amelia.kurti@dkfz-heidelberg.de", role = c("aut")),
    person("Judith", "Zaugg", email = "judith.zaugg@embl.de", role = "aut"))
Maintainer: Aryan Kamal <aryan.kamal@embl.de>
Description: Provides methods to estimate transcriptional entropy for
    individual cells in Seurat objects and AnnData h5ad files. It supports
    BUB-based and binary entropy estimation using neighborhood gene expression,
    with direct integration into R, Seurat, Python, and Scanpy workflows.
    Optional count-depth correction thins every cell to a common library
    depth before estimation, because sequencing depth inflates entropy for
    purely technical reasons. Two diagnostics assess whether a per-cell score
    is confounded: an observational screen that compares clusters at matched
    covariate values, and an interventional check that alters the input and
    recomputes entropy to ask whether the cluster ranking survives.
